// simon36_r1112.hpp - the 36x36 reproducer, frozen.
//
// The residual block of the qudit Simon post-oracle state at d=6, n=2, hidden
// period s={2,4}, after the exact site-0 peel. True spectrum: twelve singular
// values at 1/(2*sqrt(3)), the rest zero, so sum sigma^2 = 1.
//
// A LITERAL, for the same reason as poison_theta_r1151.hpp. The builder in
// diag_r1160_matrices.hpp constructs this through the library and through an
// Eigen SVD of its own, so it cannot be evaluated outside a Lindblad binary,
// and inside one every Eigen instantiation is a weak symbol the linker may
// take from a translation unit compiled under different FP flags. A run there
// cannot say which FP model produced its result. A literal can be handed to a
// single-TU program where that question has an answer.
//
// Captured at 1.1.24.0 on Eigen 3.4.0. Emitted with %a, so exact.
//
// The content is worth knowing before reading a failure: the imaginary part is
// identically zero, so this complex matrix is real, and the real part holds
// only entries of magnitude 1/6 in a sparse permutation-like pattern plus a
// single -3.4e-17 at (4,0) left by the peel. Twelve groups of three 1/6 entries
// give sqrt(3)/6 = 1/(2*sqrt(3)) each, which is the expected spectrum.

